From 406777c4c0bd8d246d41d012088958fc7ad3902d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ericman2001 <ericman2001@hotmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:35:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 04/17] phy: qcom: eusb2-repeater: Reset the repeater on init

The driver only ever sets EUSB2_RPTR_EN. On the HP Googlebook (Quartz),
the firmware leaves the SMB2360 repeaters enabled, and depthcharge stops
the xHCI controller at handoff while a device may be attached. The
repeater of that port then never passes the port's USB 2.0 signalling
on again: the PHY sees no line state change, so nothing enumerates on
that port until reboot, not even after replugging or rebinding the
controller.

Toggle the enable off and on before programming the repeater, as the
firmware (coreboot) does, so it starts from a clean state.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-eusb2-repeater.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-eusb2-repeater.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-eusb2-repeater.c
index efeec4709..ba3ceb54c 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-eusb2-repeater.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-eusb2-repeater.c
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
  * Copyright (c) 2023, Linaro Limited
  */
 
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/regulator/consumer.h>
@@ -154,6 +155,14 @@ static int eusb2_repeater_init(struct phy *phy)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * Reset the repeater by toggling its enable, as the firmware does.
+	 * Otherwise a repeater that was left enabled with a device attached
+	 * (e.g. by a bootloader that stopped the host controller mid-session)
+	 * never sees that port's USB 2.0 signalling again.
+	 */
+	regmap_write(regmap, base + EUSB2_EN_CTL1, 0);
+	udelay(50);
 	regmap_write(regmap, base + EUSB2_EN_CTL1, EUSB2_RPTR_EN);
 
 	/* Write registers from init table */
-- 
